    <!-- 1 POLES & FORCES -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="polesforce">
      <span class="tag lo">Poles &amp; forces</span>
      <h2>Two poles, a non-contact force</h2>
      <p>Every magnet has two <b>poles</b>: a <span class="hl t">north (N)</span> and a <span class="hl k">south (S)</span>. The force between them is a <b>non-contact force</b> — it acts without the magnets touching:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Like poles repel</b> (N–N or S–S push apart).</li>
        <li><b>Unlike poles attract</b> (N–S pull together).</li>
        <li>The force is <b>strongest</b> at the poles, where the field is most concentrated.</li>
      </ul>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 140" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Like poles repel, unlike poles attract">
          <rect x="40" y="30" width="55" height="34" fill="#2e8bff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="67" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">S</text>
          <rect x="95" y="30" width="55" height="34" fill="#ff5b6e" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="122" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">N</text>
          <rect x="200" y="30" width="55" height="34" fill="#ff5b6e" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="227" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">N</text>
          <g stroke="#ff5b6e" stroke-width="3"><line x1="158" y1="47" x2="178" y2="47"/><line x1="180" y1="47" x2="160" y2="47"/></g>
          <polygon points="158,47 170,42 170,52" fill="#ff5b6e"/><polygon points="198,47 186,42 186,52" fill="#ff5b6e"/>
          <text x="178" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#c8203a">like → repel</text>
          <rect x="320" y="30" width="55" height="34" fill="#ff5b6e" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="347" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">N</text>
          <rect x="455" y="30" width="55" height="34" fill="#2e8bff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="482" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">S</text>
          <polygon points="412,47 400,42 400,52" fill="#34c777"/><polygon points="418,47 430,42 430,52" fill="#34c777"/>
          <line x1="378" y1="47" x2="408" y2="47" stroke="#34c777" stroke-width="3"/><line x1="422" y1="47" x2="452" y2="47" stroke="#34c777" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="415" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#137a45">unlike → attract</text>
        </svg>
      </figure>
      <p class="note"><b>Magnetic materials:</b> the magnetic metals are <b>iron, steel, cobalt and nickel</b>. Most other metals (like copper or aluminium) are <b>not</b> magnetic.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2 Q: poles MCQ -->
    <section class="screen" data-test="polesforce">
      <span class="tag">Quick check</span>
      <h2>Which way is the force?</h2>
      <div class="activity">
        <div class="qline"><span class="qnum">?</span><span>The <b>N pole</b> of one bar magnet is brought close to the <b>N pole</b> of another. What happens, and what type of force is it?</span></div>
        <div class="opts" data-q="q1" data-why="Like poles repel, and magnetism acts through the air without the magnets touching — so it is a non-contact force.">
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">They attract; a contact force <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="1">They repel; a non-contact force <span class="mk">✅</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">They attract; a non-contact force <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">Nothing happens unless they touch <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="fb-q1"></div>
      </div>
